WEBVTT

00:00:08.704 --> 00:00:10.706
[♪♪♪]

00:00:19.889 --> 00:00:23.240
WOMAN:
I killed Sirius Black!

00:00:23.284 --> 00:00:25.025
[WOMAN CACKLES]

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:29.725
MAN:
He's back.

00:00:29.768 --> 00:00:31.640
[MAN YELLS]

00:01:27.565 --> 00:01:29.567
[♪♪♪]

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:08.780
[PEOPLE SCREAMING]

00:02:17.398 --> 00:02:19.400
[CHATTERING]

00:02:27.321 --> 00:02:29.410
[METAL SQUEAKING]

00:02:31.151 --> 00:02:32.848
[PEOPLE SCREAMING]

00:02:53.477 --> 00:02:56.393
MAN [ON RADIO]:
The police are continuing
with the investigation

00:02:56.437 --> 00:02:58.569
into the cause of
the Millennium Bridge disaster.

00:02:58.613 --> 00:03:02.530
Traffic has been halted
as police search for survivors.

00:03:02.573 --> 00:03:04.227
The surrounding area
remains closed.

00:03:04.271 --> 00:03:07.187
The mayor has urged Londoners
to remain calm....

00:03:12.235 --> 00:03:14.237
"Harry Potter."

00:03:14.281 --> 00:03:16.370
Who's Harry Potter?

00:03:17.893 --> 00:03:20.461
Oh, no one.

00:03:20.504 --> 00:03:21.897
Bit of a tosser, really.

00:03:24.247 --> 00:03:26.118
Funny, that paper of yours.

00:03:26.162 --> 00:03:28.643
Couple nights ago, I could've
sworn I saw a picture move.

00:03:28.686 --> 00:03:29.861
Really?

00:03:29.905 --> 00:03:32.212
Thought I was going
around the twist.

00:03:38.348 --> 00:03:39.567
Hey, I was wondering--

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:43.048
Eleven. That's when I get off.

00:03:43.092 --> 00:03:46.095
You can tell me all about
that tosser Harry Potter.

00:04:08.683 --> 00:04:10.728
[♪♪♪]

00:04:36.798 --> 00:04:39.279
DUMBLEDORE:
You've been reckless
this summer, Harry.

00:04:39.322 --> 00:04:42.499
HARRY:
I like riding around on trains.

00:04:42.543 --> 00:04:44.806
Takes my mind off things.

00:04:46.155 --> 00:04:48.288
Rather unpleasant
to behold, isn't it?

00:04:48.331 --> 00:04:51.769
The tale is thrilling,
if I say so myself.

00:04:51.813 --> 00:04:54.424
But now is not
the time to tell it.

00:04:54.468 --> 00:04:56.252
Take my arm.

00:04:59.299 --> 00:05:01.170
Do as I say.

00:05:10.092 --> 00:05:11.659
I just Apparated, didn't I?

00:05:11.702 --> 00:05:15.053
Indeed. Quite successfully too,
I might add.

00:05:15.097 --> 00:05:17.882
Most people vomit
the first time.

00:05:17.926 --> 00:05:19.797
I can't imagine why.

00:05:27.327 --> 00:05:31.331
DUMBLEDORE:
Welcome to the charming village
of Budleigh Babberton.

00:05:31.374 --> 00:05:32.941
Harry, I assume,
right about now,

00:05:32.984 --> 00:05:35.683
you must be wondering
why I brought you here.

00:05:35.726 --> 00:05:37.554
Am I right?

00:05:37.598 --> 00:05:39.382
Actually, sir,
after all these years,

00:05:39.426 --> 00:05:41.166
I just sort of go with it.

00:05:45.519 --> 00:05:47.521
Wands out, Harry.

00:05:49.087 --> 00:05:51.089
[♪♪♪]

00:05:58.706 --> 00:06:00.360
[WHISPERING]
Horace?

00:06:12.459 --> 00:06:13.938
Horace?

